+RE4 JPN RNG / Input / Drop Tracer v2 for Dolphin
+=================================================
+
+Target
+------
+Game ID: G4BJ08 (Biohazard 4 JPN)
+RNG function: 0x8014BDA0
+Global 16-bit RNG state: 0x802B69BC
+
+Files produced
+--------------
+<Dolphin User Folder>/Logs/re4_jpn_rng_trace.csv
+  External RNG callers only. call_index still counts every RNG entry, including
+  internal calls, so RNG agenda offsets remain measurable without huge files.
+
+<Dolphin User Folder>/Logs/re4_jpn_pad_trace.csv
+  One row for every controller-1 poll delivered to the game, even when no RNG
+  call happens. This resolves timing ambiguities between nearby movie inputs.
+
+<Dolphin User Folder>/Logs/re4_jpn_drop_trace.csv
+  Register snapshots at known RE4 JPN drop-related PCs. Each row contains:
+  frame/input/poll, PC/label, seed, LR/CTR/CR/XER, controller state, and r0-r31.
+
+Drop probes
+-----------
+0x800D1978  drop path checkpoint
+0x800D1B34  drop path checkpoint
+0x800D1E9C  grenade type roll
+0x800D1EF0  grenade final-ID checkpoint
+0x800D224C  ammo/item path
+0x800D23F8  quantity checkpoint
+0x800D24B8  drop path checkpoint
+0x800D2770  drop path checkpoint
+0x800D2794  drop gate RNG call
+0x800D2798  immediately after drop-gate RNG
+0x800D27B0  drop path checkpoint
+0x800D2B64  selected drop path
+0x800D2BF0  ammo path checkpoint
+0x800D2FC0  late drop RNG checkpoint
+0x800D2FD0  late drop RNG call
+0x800D2FE0  late result pre-checkpoint
+0x800D2FE4  late result checkpoint
+0x800D2FF8  final return checkpoint
+
+Notes
+-----
+The labels describe our current reverse-engineering checkpoints; the raw PPC
+register dump is the source of truth. The first v2 tests with known outcomes
+(incendiary grenade and 10 handgun ammo) can be used to identify which register
+carries the final item ID and quantity at the labeled checkpoints.
+
+CPU cores
+---------
+- x86-64 JIT: supported (normal Windows x64 Dolphin path)
+- Interpreter: supported
+- Cached Interpreter / ARM64 JIT: not instrumented by this patch
